{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.P5Counterexample","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.P5Counterexample","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.ns_counterexample_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.ns_counterexample_holds","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L62-L62","doc":"**The conjecture itself.**  The velocity is unbounded as\n$t \\to T^{*-}$: on *every* left neighbourhood of $T^*$ it exceeds\nevery bound $M$.\n\nThe `T* - ε < t` conjunct is what puts the blow-up *at* $T^*$ and\nis not optional: without it the field says only that the velocity\nis unbounded somewhere on $t < T^*$, which is satisfied by\n`velocityProfile t x = max (-t) 0` with `T* = 1` — a profile that\ntends to $0$ as $t \\to T^{*-}$ and so exhibits no finite-time\nsingularity at all (verified counterexample:\n`docs/audits/2026-08-29-q-ns-conjecture-statement-strength-probe.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.singularityTime_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.singularityTime_pos","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Singularity time is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.velocityProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.velocityProfile","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The velocity profile $u : \\mathrm{time} \\to \\mathrm{space} \\to \\mathbb{R}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.singularityTime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.singularityTime","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L45-L45","doc":"A finite singularity time $T^* > 0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.NSCounterexample","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.lean#L38-L65","doc":"**`conj:ns-counterexample` (axiomatised).**\n\nThe classical limit $q \\to 1$ of the $q$-NS evolution admits a\nfinite-time singularity: a concrete velocity profile $u(t, x)$\nand time $T^*$ at which $\\sup_x |u(t, x)|$ blows up. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:ns-counterexample","label":"conj:ns-counterexample","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p5-counterexample.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}